 {
  "id": "G025",
  "article_id": "gnews:c3c81e4fb573a723e4081dd0",
  "title": "One of America's oldest manufacturers says AI is creating jobs — not replacing them",
  "publication_day": "2026-07-01",
  "article_opening": "By Amanda Macias Fox News\nInside Corning's North Carolina factory, workers are producing the optical fiber that has become a critical piece of the infrastructure powering the AI boom. (Footage courtesy of Corning)\nBefore Henry Ford rolled out the Model T, before the Wright brothers took to the skies and before the Statue of Liberty welcomed millions to America's shores, Corning was already charting a course of innovation that continues today.\nBest known to many Americans for the glass products t",
  "passage": "…tical manufacturing capacity tenfold.\nHaving worked with innovators such as Apple co-founder Steve Jobs during his career, Weeks said he's proud to now partner with NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang as Corning helps build the infrastructure powering the AI revolution.\nWhile companies like NVIDIA have become synonymous with artificial intelligence, Weeks said many people overlook the role optical fiber plays in connecting AI systems.\n\"The common story is AI being powered by chips, but actually, those chips are connected by glass,\" Weeks said.\nThe AI manufacturing boom isn't just fueling growth at longtime American companies like Corning. It's also attracting foreign investment into U.S. manufacturing. Wistron, a Taiwan-based electronics manufacturer, is establishing AI supercomputer manufacturing operations in Texas for NVIDIA, bringing advanced manufacturing jobs to the state.\n\"Building in America is essential for speed, resilience and strategic advantage,\" Wistron Chairman Simon Lin told Fox News Digital.\n\"Texas offers the talent, industrial strength, and strategic location to help power the next generation of AI infrastructure, while creating durable, high-value jobs at scale for the local workforce,\" he added.\nAs America marks 250 years of independence, Weeks said the country's next chapter of innovation will depend not only on breakthrough ideas, but on manufacturing them at home.\n\"The tools change, but the approach doesn't,\" Weeks said.\nAmanda Macias covers the intersection of business, economics and politi…",
  "statement": "Wistron, a Taiwan-based electronics manufacturer, is establishing AI supercomputer manufacturing operations in Texas for NVIDIA"
 },
 {
  "id": "G109",
  "article_id": "gnews:3345f0d91321165a099860c9",
  "title": "Singapore Seizes $42M Mansion in Nvidia Chip Smuggling Probe｜Daily News Digest｜2026-07-02｜web only",
  "publication_day": "2026-07-02",
  "article_opening": "Singapore Seizes $42M Mansion in Nvidia Chip Smuggling Probe\nJuly 2, 2026 -- Today’s top stories: Singapore Seizes $42M Mansion in Nvidia Chip Smuggling Probe, Rubio Would Step Aside for Vance in 2028 White House Race, and Google Ordered To Pay Klarna $1.97b in Antitrust Damages.\nBy CommonWealth Magazine\nSingapore seizes $42m home in Nvidia chip smuggling case\nSingapore authorities have seized a multimillion-dollar mansion and charged people with money laundering as part of a case of suspected c",
  "passage": "…ntaining Nvidia chips.\nA prohibition of disposal order was issued against the luxury home, valued at about SGD 55M ($42M), freezing the asset and preventing its purchase or sale. Funds in bank accounts under investigation, valued at about SGD 1M, were also seized.\nLim Jenny and Woon Guo Jie Aaron, two people suspected of involvement in the alleged smuggling, face money laundering charges. Four firms allegedly linked to the export of computer servers that might contain Nvidia chips to Malaysia are facing charges for false representation.\nThe companies are Aperia International, A-Speed Infotech, and Aperia Cloud Services (II) — collectively known as the Aperia group — and Luxuriate Your Life.\nThis comes after a US investigation into whether Chinese start-up Deepseek had circumvented US restrictions on advanced Nvidia chips by buying them from third parties in other countries, including Singapore.\nLuxuriate Your Life was charged on July 1, while the other three firms will be charged on July 6.\nThree individuals were also hauled to court on July 1 and charged with various offences, including fraud and money laundering.\nRubio would step aside for Vance in 2028 White House race\nUS Secretary of State Marco Rubio will not run for the Republican nomination for US president in the 2028 election if Vice President JD Vance announces such an intention, according to the Associated Press.\nRubio has repeatedly mentioned in conversations with his advisers and aides his intention to make way for Vanc…",
  "statement": "This comes after a US investigation into whether Chinese start-up Deepseek had circumvented US restrictions"
 },
 {
  "id": "G536",
  "article_id": "gnews:dbff79c9778e4b3d8ac8eef2",
  "title": "Nokia advances AI-RAN toward commercial deployment and physical AI, launches sovereign agentic AI platform for telco autonomy with NVIDIA",
  "publication_day": "2026-10-21",
  "article_opening": "Nokia advances AI-RAN toward commercial deployment and physical AI, launches sovereign agentic AI platform for telco autonomy with NVIDIA\nNew capabilities improve radio performance, enable real-time intelligence at the edge and extend governed AI agents across network operations.\nNokia AI-native anyRAN software and NVIDIA accelerated computing turn the radio access network into a distributed platform for sensing, intelligence and real-time action.\nBT, Deutsche Telekom, Elisa and Orange provide g",
  "passage": "…ational context and governance needed for agents to understand network conditions and take controlled action. Glass-box autonomy maintains operator oversight, while agentic guardrails govern how actions are tested and executed.\nThe combined architecture, integrated with NVIDIA open models and libraries, supports on-premises, cloud and hybrid deployments, giving operators control over where operational data, models and policies reside. It extends the Nokia and NVIDIA collaboration from AI in the radio network to autonomous operations, creating a common foundation to optimize the RAN, support AI workloads close to where data is generated and enable low-latency autonomy across network domains. Several telecommunication providers, including etisalat UAE, MEO and Airtel, are working with Nokia to identify advanced use cases and integration timelines.\nHigh-performance solutions that link distributed AI infrastructure\nAt GTC, Nokia will also showcase high-performance IP and optical solutions required to link distributed AI infrastructure. Nokia’s data center connectivity, IP gateway and wide-area networking solutions, including 800G coherent pluggables, help cloud and AI builders scale connectivity across a diverse and growing set of data center locations. By connecting radio, edge and data-center resources as one coordinated infrastructure environment, Nokia’s technology supports AI workloads everywhere.\nMultimedia, technical information, and related news\nPress release: NVIDIA, Nokia and Europe’s leading telecom operators turn networks i…",
  "statement": "Several telecommunication providers, including etisalat UAE, MEO and Airtel, are working with Nokia to identify advanced use cases and integration timelines."
 },
 {
  "id": "G153",
  "article_id": "gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568",
  "title": "Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?",
  "publication_day": "2026-07-04",
  "article_opening": "Nvidia (NASDAQ: NVDA) investors have had it good for several years. In 2023, 2024, and 2025, it produced market-crushing returns, making it one of the best stocks to own during each of those years. However, 2026 hasn't been that way. The stock is up 5% so far in 2026, which isn't nothing, but compared to the returns that Nvidia investors have enjoyed in recent years, it feels like an absolute failure. On another note, its market-crushing status is in jeopardy for 2026, as the S&P 500 is up nearl",
  "passage": "…ct line has become the go-to for several AI hyperscalers and cloud providers. Nvidia has a complete ecosystem of products that gives its clients everything they need to run an Nvidia-powered data center, locking in clients once they've chosen to use its products.\nThis bodes well for the future, as AI hyperscalers are spending a massive amount of money this year and beyond to continue building out their AI computing footprints. The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year. Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion. That means more growth is coming to Nvidia, and the investing story is far from complete. Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year, so there's another external source that's projecting even more growth for Nvidia.\nHowever, the stock price doesn't reflect that.\nNvidia trades at 21.7 times forward earnings, essentially the same price tag as the S&P 500. This conveys that the market believes Nvidia will be a market-average stock after 2026's growth is accounted for. However, Wall Street analysts don't believe that, as they're guiding for major growth next year. That's why the stock looks so cheap when next year's earnings are used to value the stock.\nAs a result, I think Nvidia is an excellent stock to buy now. None of next year's growth has been priced in, which could lead to strong returns toward the end of this year.",
  "statement": "Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year"
 },
 {
  "id": "G031",
  "article_id": "gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45",
  "title": "NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.",
  "publication_day": "2026-07-01",
